cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "cascade" in publications use:'
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
title: 'cascade: Contextualizing Untargeted Annotation with Semi-Quantitative Charged
  Aerosol Detection for Pertinent Characterization of Natural Extracts'
version: 0.0.0.9003
abstract: Provides the infrastructure to perform Automated Composition Assessment
  of Natural Extracts by combining untargeted mass spectrometry feature tables and
  taxonomically informed metabolite annotations (TIMA) with semi-quantitative universal
  detectors such as Charged Aerosol Detection (CAD) and Photodiode Array (PDA) chromatograms.
  Includes Fourier filtering, derivative-based peak sharpening, peak integration,
  extracted ion chromatogram correlation, Wikidata/LOTUS chemotaxonomic literature
  queries, and interactive visualizations.
